PHASE 31: PAPER TRADING ENGINE MIGRATION — COMPLETE ARCHITECTURE & IMPLEMENTATION REPORT
Classification: Principal Systems Architecture

Date: 2026-06-06

Audience: Senior Go engineers, trading infrastructure team

Status: Actionable — Implementation-ready

EXECUTIVE SUMMARY
The paper trading engine currently operates across three execution tiers: a browser-hosted React strategy engine (useBTCFuturesScalperEngine.ts, 170 KB), a Node.js VPS worker (runPaperDeskPollTick.ts, 900 lines), and a Vercel 60-second cron fallback. The Go backend already contains a fully-featured $1M paper account with 600+ live strategies, deterministic OMS, risk gate, kill switch, ledger, and reconciliation — but it persists state only in-process (SQLite/file fallback) and does not write trades to the paper_trades MongoDB collection the frontend reads.

The migration collapses all three tiers into one: the Go service on Render becomes the sole execution authority. The frontend becomes a pure read layer. This is achievable in 7 phases over approximately 8 weeks.

