FINAL NOTES
The Go engine already has everything needed. The 600+ strategies are running, the PaperOMS is deterministic, the risk gate is active, the kill switch is wired. The only gap is that it does not write to the MongoDB collections the frontend reads, and the frontend does not know it should stop executing its own engine.

The migration is fundamentally a plumbing job: connect the existing Go execution outputs to MongoDB persistence channels (Phase 31A), then shut down the competing execution paths (Phase 31D+), then clean up the frontend (Phase 31F).

The total lines of new Go code is approximately 800 lines across 9 files — modest relative to the existing engine scale. The SSE hub is ~120 lines. The risk is low because every phase runs in parallel with the existing system before any existing code is removed.

The result: paper trading runs 24/7 on Render with zero browser dependency, MongoDB as single source of truth, and the browser as a pure read layer.